@page "/about"

<PageTitle>About - Label Verification</PageTitle>

@*
    Evaluator- and compliance-agent-facing guidance for the prototype.

    This page intentionally explains:
    - what the prototype does
    - how automated outcomes should be interpreted
    - where human judgment remains required
    - important prototype scope and data-handling limitations
*@

<div class="container-fluid px-0">

    <header class="mb-4">
        <h1 class="mb-2">About Label Verification</h1>

        <p class="lead text-muted mb-3">
            A human-in-the-loop prototype for alcohol label verification using
            .NET 8, Blazor, Azure Document Intelligence, and deterministic
            compliance rules.
        </p>

        <div class="alert alert-primary border-0" role="note">
            <strong>Designed to assist compliance agents.</strong>
            AI and OCR extract evidence from submitted labels, while deterministic
            rules evaluate objective checks. Human reviewers retain final decision
            authority.
        </div>
    </header>

    <section class="mb-5" aria-labelledby="how-it-works-heading">
        <h2 id="how-it-works-heading" class="h4 mb-3">
            How it works
        </h2>

        <p>
            The prototype separates perception from compliance decision logic.
            Azure Document Intelligence extracts text and layout evidence from a
            label image. The application then parses that evidence and applies
            deterministic verification rules against the selected application record.
        </p>

        <div class="row g-3 mt-2">
            <div class="col-md-3">
                <div class="card h-100 shadow-sm border-0">
                    <div class="card-body">
                        <div class="fw-semibold mb-2">1. Select</div>
                        <p class="text-muted mb-0">
                            Choose the application record that represents the
                            expected approved data.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="col-md-3">
                <div class="card h-100 shadow-sm border-0">
                    <div class="card-body">
                        <div class="fw-semibold mb-2">2. Upload</div>
                        <p class="text-muted mb-0">
                            Submit one label for focused review or multiple labels
                            for bounded batch verification.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="col-md-3">
                <div class="card h-100 shadow-sm border-0">
                    <div class="card-body">
                        <div class="fw-semibold mb-2">3. Verify</div>
                        <p class="text-muted mb-0">
                            OCR extracts evidence and deterministic rules compare
                            supported fields with expected values.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="col-md-3">
                <div class="card h-100 shadow-sm border-0">
                    <div class="card-body">
                        <div class="fw-semibold mb-2">4. Review</div>
                        <p class="text-muted mb-0">
                            Inspect field-level evidence and apply human judgment
                            wherever the result requires review.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-5" aria-labelledby="results-heading">
        <h2 id="results-heading" class="h4 mb-3">
            Understanding verification results
        </h2>

        <p class="text-muted">
            Automated results are decision-support signals. They do not replace
            the compliance agent's final regulatory determination.
        </p>

        <div class="table-responsive">
            <table class="table table-bordered align-middle">
                <thead class="table-light">
                    <tr>
                        <th scope="col" style="width: 140px;">Result</th>
                        <th scope="col">What it means</th>
                        <th scope="col">Agent action</th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr>
                        <td>
                            <span class="badge bg-success">PASS</span>
                        </td>
                        <td>
                            Available evidence satisfies the implemented automated
                            verification checks.
                        </td>
                        <td>
                            Review the evidence as appropriate and continue the
                            compliance workflow.
                        </td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td>
                            <span class="badge bg-warning text-dark">REVIEW</span>
                        </td>
                        <td>
                            One or more fields contain ambiguous, incomplete, or
                            borderline evidence that should not be forced into an
                            automated determination.
                        </td>
                        <td>
                            Examine the field-level evidence and make the final
                            determination using regulatory judgment.
                        </td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td>
                            <span class="badge bg-danger">FAIL</span>
                        </td>
                        <td>
                            One or more deterministic checks clearly differ from
                            expected application data or an implemented rule.
                        </td>
                        <td>
                            Review the failed field and supporting evidence before
                            determining the appropriate compliance action.
                        </td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td>
                            <span class="badge bg-secondary">ERROR</span>
                        </td>
                        <td>
                            A technical problem prevented verification from
                            completing successfully.
                        </td>
                        <td>
                            Retry the operation or investigate the technical issue.
                            ERROR is not a regulatory failure.
                        </td>
                    </tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-5" aria-labelledby="checks-heading">
        <h2 id="checks-heading" class="h4 mb-3">
            Current verification coverage
        </h2>

        <p>
            The prototype currently evaluates supported evidence for the following
            compliance fields:
        </p>

        <ul>
            <li>Brand name, including controlled similarity handling</li>
            <li>Alcohol by volume (ABV)</li>
            <li>Proof</li>
            <li>Net contents with unit-aware comparison</li>
            <li>Government Warning wording and supported presentation evidence</li>
        </ul>

        <div class="alert alert-light border" role="note">
            <strong>Class/type:</strong>
            Class/type information may be extracted and displayed for context,
            but it is not currently included in the aggregate automated
            PASS / REVIEW / FAIL determination.
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-5" aria-labelledby="agent-guidance-heading">
        <h2 id="agent-guidance-heading" class="h4 mb-3">
            Guidance for compliance agents
        </h2>

        <div class="row g-3">
            <div class="col-lg-6">
                <div class="card h-100">
                    <div class="card-body">
                        <h3 class="h6">Use field-level evidence</h3>
                        <p class="mb-0">
                            Expand individual results when a determination is
                            unclear. The overall status should be considered
                            together with the extracted evidence and explanation
                            for each field.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="col-lg-6">
                <div class="card h-100">
                    <div class="card-body">
                        <h3 class="h6">Treat REVIEW as intentional</h3>
                        <p class="mb-0">
                            REVIEW exists to preserve human judgment when evidence
                            is ambiguous. It is not a system failure and should not
                            automatically be treated as noncompliance.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="col-lg-6">
                <div class="card h-100">
                    <div class="card-body">
                        <h3 class="h6">Keep ERROR separate from FAIL</h3>
                        <p class="mb-0">
                            Technical failures are operational conditions.
                            A label should not receive a regulatory failure merely
                            because OCR, image processing, or another technical
                            dependency could not complete.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="col-lg-6">
                <div class="card h-100">
                    <div class="card-body">
                        <h3 class="h6">Use batch mode for larger submissions</h3>
                        <p class="mb-0">
                            Batch verification processes labels independently so
                            agents can identify PASS, REVIEW, FAIL, and technical
                            ERROR results without losing visibility into individual
                            label evidence.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-4" aria-labelledby="scope-heading">
        <h2 id="scope-heading" class="h4 mb-3">
            Prototype scope and limitations
        </h2>

        <ul>
            <li>
                This prototype is a standalone demonstration and does not connect
                directly to COLA.
            </li>
            <li>
                It does not write regulatory decisions back to Treasury or TTB
                systems.
            </li>
            <li>
                AI and OCR provide perception and evidence extraction; they are
                not the regulatory authority.
            </li>
            <li>
                Deterministic rules are used for objective automated checks.
            </li>
            <li>
                Ambiguous evidence is intentionally routed to human review rather
                than forced into an unsupported automated determination.
            </li>
            <li>
                Human reviewers retain final decision authority.
            </li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-5" aria-labelledby="data-heading">
        <div class="alert alert-warning" role="note">
            <h2 id="data-heading" class="h6 alert-heading">
                Prototype data handling
            </h2>

            <p class="mb-0">
                Use synthetic or otherwise approved test data when evaluating this
                prototype. Do not upload production applicant data, personally
                identifiable information, or other sensitive information.
            </p>
        </div>
    </section>

</div>